# Paths that need the maintainer's review before a pull request touching them
# can merge, once the repository ruleset requires code-owner review (R27).
#
# release.yml runs with the certificate, the notarization key and, later, the
# appcast key. The constraints written into it hold only for as long as nobody
# can edit them away unreviewed. The packaging scripts decide what gets signed,
# checked and published, so they are protected the same way.
/.github/                @Facens
/packaging/              @Facens
# The entry points those workflows execute: make test, make bundle, and the
# manifest check-source.sh dumps.
/Makefile                @Facens
/Package.swift           @Facens
